1
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:11,790
To my wife, Erika.
致我的妻子埃里卡。

2
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:16,550
Erika, thank you so much.
埃里卡，非常感谢你。

3
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:20,950
You know, I have to first have to say thank you to my wife.
你知道，我首先必须向我的妻子表示感谢。

4
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:36,330
It's been her strength, her resilience that have propelled me and this campaign through our hardest days.
正是她的力量和韧性推动我和这场竞选活动度过了最艰难的日子。

5
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:48,460
And I am so blessed to have you by my side, and I can't wait for Wisconsin to get to know you as their Next first lady.
我很幸运有你在我身边，我迫不及待地想让威斯康星州认识你作为他们的下一个第一夫人。

6
00:00:48,470 --> 00:01:03,510
To To our three beautiful daughters, Alyssa, Ava, Autumn.
致我们三个美丽的女儿，Alyssa、Ava、Autumn。

7
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,455
We call them the a squad, y'all.
我们称他们为小队，你们大家。

8
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:13,395
And I want to let them know that nothing in my life makes me more proud of being their dad.
我想让他们知道，在我的生活中，没有什么比作为他们的父亲更让我感到自豪的了。

9
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:18,320
Thank you for believing in me as much as I believe in you.
谢谢你对我的信任，就像我对你的信任一样。

10
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:23,640
And I hope that they see tonight that no matter the setbacks that life throws you,
我希望今晚他们能够看到，无论生活给你带来什么挫折，

11
00:01:24,127 --> 00:01:27,528
If you work hard and be kind, anything is possible.
如果你努力工作并且善良，一切皆有可能。

12
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:31,310
I love you guys.
我爱你们。

13
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,360
And I would not be here.
我不会在这里。

14
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:41,960
I would not be the man I am today if it was not for my parents.
如果没有我的父母，我就不会成为今天的我。

15
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:47,140
So, I want to say thank you to my father, David, my stepmother,
所以，我想对我的父亲、大卫、我的继母说声谢谢，

16
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,220
Beth, for their unwavering love and support.
贝丝，感谢他们坚定不移的爱和支持。

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,900
But, I also want to give a special thank you to my mother, Valerie.
但是，我还要特别感谢我的妈妈，瓦莱丽.

18
00:01:56,591 --> 00:02:08,240
It was her determination and grace that made it life so much more possible.
正是她的决心和优雅让生活变得更加可能。

19
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:14,240
And while I wish she was here tonight, I know that she is proud of what we've been able to build together,
虽然我希望她今晚也在这里，但我知道她为我们共同创造的一切感到自豪，

20
00:02:16,551 --> 00:02:16,886
Y'all.
你们大家。

21
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:27,550
And to the incredible sara godlewski, our next lieutenant governor, you know I hit the jackpot with this one on the campaign.
对于令人难以置信的下一任副州长萨拉·戈德莱夫斯基（sara godlewski），你知道我在竞选中凭借这一点赢得了大奖。

22
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:36,560
And I know the same will be true while we're governing, and I can't wait to get to work with you for the people
我知道在我们执政期间也是如此，我迫不及待地想与您一起为人民服务

23
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:37,580
Of this great state.
属于这个伟大的国家。

24
00:02:38,892 --> 00:02:44,520
And to the man that I look up to personally and professionally, our great Governor Tony Evers.
感谢我在个人和职业上尊敬的人，我们伟大的州长托尼·埃弗斯。

25
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:55,030
For 8 years, you and your team fought every single day to make life better for our friends and for our neighbors.
8年来，您和您的团队每天都在为让我们的朋友和邻居生活得更好而奋斗。

26
00:02:56,710 --> 00:03:02,450
Governor, I am proud to call you my friend, honored to have had your support in my campaign,
州长，我很自豪地称你为我的朋友，很荣幸在我的竞选活动中得到你的支持，

27
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:08,050
And I will build on what you have been doing and have done to keep moving the great state of Wisconsin forward.
我将在你们一直在做的事情和已经做的事情的基础上继续推动伟大的威斯康星州向前发展。

28
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:09,490
And so, thank you.
所以，谢谢。

29
00:03:09,490 --> 00:03:16,930
To not just our great Governor, but also to Kathy Evers for all that you have done and sacrificed for the great people of This state.
不仅感谢我们伟大的州长，也感谢凯西·埃弗斯 (Kathy Evers)，感谢您为伟大的人民所做的一切和牺牲本州。

30
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:28,760
This win belongs to the volunteers who knocked doors in the rain and the cold.
这场胜利属于在风雨中、在寒冷中敲门的志愿者们。

31
00:03:34,694 --> 00:03:38,920
To the union members who spent their precious time walking their own neighborhoods,
对于那些花费宝贵时间在自己的社区散步的工会成员，

32
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:49,000
To the staff that gave their campaign a year of their lives, and to everyone here and beyond who chipped in five bucks because They believed.
感谢那些为他们的竞选活动付出了一年生命的工作人员，以及这里和其他地方的每个人，因为他们捐了五块钱他们相信。

33
00:03:50,020 --> 00:04:00,086
And I especially want to thank my campaign manager Garren Randolph, who was the loyal and steady hand guiding this campaign from the very Beginning.
我特别要感谢我的竞选经理加伦·兰道夫 (Garren Randolph)，他从一开始就忠实而稳定地指导了这次竞选活动。开始。

34
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:03,150
But this win also belongs to Milwaukee.
但这场胜利也属于密尔沃基。

35
00:04:03,894 --> 00:04:09,547
The city that raised me.
这座养育我的城市。

36
00:04:09,557 --> 00:04:21,080
It belongs to Milwaukee, the city that raised me, and to every corner of this state that showed up tonight.
它属于密尔沃基，这座养育我的城市，属于今晚出现的本州的每一个角落。

37
00:04:22,494 --> 00:04:29,880
And to everyone who started this year backing someone else and finished it on our team.
感谢今年开始支持其他人并在我们团队中完成这一工作的每个人。

38
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,520
Thank you.
谢谢你。

39
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:35,200
We are stronger because you are here.
因为有你在，我们更强大。

40
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:36,120
Thank you.
谢谢你。

41
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:44,920
And I would be remiss if I did not say thank you to the clerks and to the poll workers who worked before sunrise
如果我不向日出前工作的职员和投票站工作人员表示感谢，那就是我的失职

42
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,860
Until the last ballot was counted.
直到最后一张选票清点完毕。

43
00:04:47,378 --> 00:04:49,444
Thank you for your hard work.
感谢您的辛勤工作。

44
00:04:49,454 --> 00:04:55,644
Thank you for participating in our democracy.
感谢您参与我们的民主。

45
00:04:55,654 --> 00:05:00,164
A few minutes ago, I had the opportunity to talk to Congressman Tom Tiffany.
几分钟前，我有机会与国会议员汤姆·蒂芙尼交谈。

46
00:05:00,164 --> 00:05:04,390
And I thank him for a hard-fought race and for his service.
我感谢他这场艰苦的比赛和他的服务。

47
00:05:05,270 --> 00:05:11,410
But despite our differences I've never doubted that he loves the state that we both call home.
但尽管我们存在分歧，我从未怀疑过他热爱我们都称之为家的州。

48
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:18,760
Finally, to the people of Wisconsin tonight is for all of you.
最后，今晚对威斯康星州人民来说是为了你们所有人。

49
00:05:19,643 --> 00:05:24,044
This is for all of you.
这是给你们所有人的。

50
00:05:24,054 --> 00:05:26,800
And you know I always say that every day is a good day,
你知道我总是说每一天都是美好的一天

51
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:31,004
But Wisconsin, this is a very good day.
但威斯康星州，这是非常好的一天。

52
00:05:31,014 --> 00:05:43,250
This is a very good because of you, a boy who grew up facing eviction will now live in the governor's residence.
多亏了你，这真是一件好事，一个在被驱逐中长大的男孩现在住在州长官邸。

53
00:05:43,878 --> 00:05:52,884
Tonight, Wisconsin made history.
今晚，威斯康星州创造了历史。

54
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:57,000
And being your next governor is humbling in its own right.
成为下一任州长本身就是一种谦卑。

55
00:05:58,934 --> 00:06:01,364
I don't take any of this lightly.
我不会掉以轻心。

56
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,820
And I know exactly the shoulders that I stand on.
我清楚地知道我所站在的肩膀上。

57
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:07,720
And I want to say thank you for placing your faith in me.
我想说谢谢你们对我的信任。

58
00:06:09,175 --> 00:06:11,940
That's ultimately what voting is.
这就是投票的最终意义。

59
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:14,740
A tremendous act of faith.
这是一个伟大的信仰之举。

60
00:06:15,815 --> 00:06:20,700
Not faith in one person or party, but faith in the idea that elections matter.
不是对某个人或某个政党的信仰，而是对选举重要这一理念的信仰。

61
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:24,280
That the right leadership can make a difference in people's lives.
正确的领导可以改变人们的生活。

62
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:32,360
Because when you're sitting around the kitchen table at night having to decide which of your bills will go past due that month.
因为当您晚上坐在厨房的桌子旁时，必须决定哪些账单将在该月到期。

63
00:06:33,335 --> 00:06:34,380
Or when your kid is sick.
或者当你的孩子生病时。

64
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:43,150
And your or parent needs care taking, but your job doesn't afford the leave for those that you love.
你或父母需要照顾，但你的工作无法为你所爱的人提供假期。

65
00:06:44,815 --> 00:06:47,730
When a family moves off a farm not because they want to leave,
当一个家庭搬离农场并不是因为他们想离开

66
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:49,710
But because they don't see a future in staying.
但因为他们看不到留下来的未来。

67
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:53,550
You don't really care about the letter that's behind the candidate's name.
你并不真正关心候选人名字后面的字母。

68
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:59,085
You just want to know that those who in power that they see you.
你只是想知道那些掌权的人看到了你。

69
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:01,970
And that they're doing everything in their power to actually deliver.
他们正在尽一切努力来实际交付。

70
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:09,019
And I just want you to know that is exactly what we're going to do for the people of the great state of Wisconsin.
我只想让你们知道，这正是我们将为伟大的威斯康星州人民所做的事情。

71
00:07:09,029 --> 00:07:14,765
But I want to be very clear.
但我想说得很清楚。

72
00:07:14,775 --> 00:07:17,400
When I say we, I don't just mean Democrats.
当我说我们时，我不仅仅指民主党。

73
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:26,100
I mean we as public servants of both parties who have been elected to work together on your behalf.
我的意思是，我们作为两党的公务员，被选举出来为你们共同努力。

74
00:07:27,255 --> 00:07:32,260
I ran to be a governor for all of us and tonight that includes everyone who didn't vote for me.
我竞选州长是为了我们所有人，今晚包括所有没有投票给我的人。

75
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,260
I want you to know that I'm going to listen to you.
我想让你知道我会听你的。

76
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:37,240
That I'm going to work for you.
我将为你工作。

77
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:45,140
And I hope to earn your trust the best way that I know how and that's by showing up and by delivering results.
我希望以我所知道的最好方式赢得您的信任，那就是通过展示和交付成果。

78
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:50,760
I stand here tonight.
今晚我站在这里。

79
00:07:53,095 --> 00:07:55,080
I stand here tonight with deep gratitude.
今晚我站在这里，怀着深深的感激之情。

80
00:07:56,280 --> 00:08:03,460
Believing more than ever that what unites us as Wisconsinites is so much bigger than what divides us.
比以往任何时候都更加相信，威斯康星州人的团结远大于分裂。

81
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:08,220
We love our families and our communities no matter how big or how small.
我们爱我们的家庭和社区，无论大小。

82
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:13,937
We believe in hard work and that our kids tomorrow can be brighter than our today.
我们相信努力工作，我们的孩子的明天会比今天更美好。

83
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:19,232
And whatever else we argue about, I do believe that we will always bleed green and gold.
无论我们争论什么，我确实相信我们将永远流着绿色和金色的血。

84
00:08:19,232 --> 00:08:25,655
And thanks to the Milwaukee Brewers, each and every one of us in this room and beyond are world champions.
感谢密尔沃基酿酒人队，我们在座内外的每一个人都是世界冠军。

85
00:08:25,665 --> 00:08:42,960
It isn't partisan to want good public schools where every child is safe and loved and on a path of success.
想要好的公立学校让每个孩子都安全、受到爱护并走上成功之路并不是党派之争。

86
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:48,000
Republican voters are worried about what they pay for health care.
共和党选民担心他们为医疗保健支付的费用。

87
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:53,340
And there are Democratic voters who want us to be sound stewards of their tax dollars.
还有一些民主党选民希望我们成为他们税款的健全管家。

88
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:59,640
At the gas pump or at the checkout line, nobody asks whether you're a Democrat or Republican.
在加油站或结账处，没有人问你是民主党人还是共和党人。

89
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,720
Those bills, they hit all of us the same.
这些账单对我们所有人来说都是同样的打击。

90
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:03,620
And you know what?
你知道吗？

91
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,300
I get it.
我得到它。

92
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:08,447
My daddy was a ibew master electrician.
我爸爸是一位 ibew 电工大师。

93
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,744
My mother, she was a jack of all trades.
我的母亲，她是个多才多艺的人。

94
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:16,140
And yet, growing up, there were nights where I didn't know if there would be food on the table,
然而，在成长的过程中，有些夜晚我不知道桌上是否有食物，

95
00:09:16,647 --> 00:09:21,807
Days where I couldn't go or be able to get to go to school because I couldn't afford the bus fare.
由于付不起公交车费，我无法去或无法去上学的日子。

96
00:09:21,807 --> 00:09:29,300
I grew up in one of those families not knowing if there would be a roof over your head or if the next doctor's
我在这样的家庭中长大，不知道自己是否有栖身之所，也不知道下一位医生是否会成为一名医生。

97
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:37,260
Bill would wipe away your finances, hoping that someone in charge would give families like ours a fighting chance.
比尔会毁掉你的财务，希望有人能给像我们这样的家庭一个奋斗的机会。

98
00:09:38,657 --> 00:09:43,240
So, to all of those families who are watching tonight, I see you.
所以，对于今晚观看比赛的所有家庭，我看到你们了。

99
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,280
I hear you.
我听到了。

100
00:09:46,257 --> 00:09:47,450
I was you.
我就是你。

101
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:54,041
And now, I'm going to fight for you each and every single day.
现在，我将每天为你而战。

102
00:09:59,410 --> 00:10:02,230
Now, there's going to be folks who are going to look at today's results.
现在，将会有人关注今天的结果。

103
00:10:03,190 --> 00:10:06,550
And they're going to see a closely divided state.
他们将看到一个严重分裂的国家。

104
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:13,528
They'll shade the map red and blue until you one color came out on top.
他们会将地图着色为红色和蓝色，直到一种颜色出现在顶部。

105
00:10:13,528 --> 00:10:16,088
But I see something different, y'all.
但我看到了一些不同的东西，你们大家。

106
00:10:16,098 --> 00:10:19,250
Wisconsin isn't a red state or a blue state.
威斯康星州既不是红州，也不是蓝州。

107
00:10:19,730 --> 00:10:22,088
We never have been.
我们从来没有去过。

108
00:10:22,098 --> 00:10:25,930
And it's In a state this close, nobody gets to govern alone.
在如此紧密的状态下，没有人能够单独执政。

109
00:10:26,590 --> 00:10:31,030
When majorities are narrow, there's no room for showboats, for shouting matches.
当多数票数过少时，就没有炫耀和争吵的空间。

110
00:10:31,630 --> 00:10:37,070
There's no time to waste on culture wars that make for great Instagram clips for lousy government.
我们没有时间浪费在文化战争上，因为文化战争会为糟糕的政府带来精彩的 Instagram 视频。

111
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:40,128
There's only room for the work.
只剩下工作的空间了。

112
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:48,575
Fixing the damn roads, funding the schools, keeping our communities safe, and bringing down your monthly bills.
修复该死的道路，为学校提供资金，保证我们社区的安全，并减少每月的账单。

113
00:10:49,112 --> 00:10:54,680
In a state like ours, the voters keep everybody honest.
在我们这样的州，选民让每个人都保持诚实。

114
00:10:55,560 --> 00:11:02,000
And tonight, they told all of us in both parties, "We are sending you to Madison to get something done.
今晚，他们告诉我们两党所有人，“我们将派你们去麦迪逊完成一些事情。

115
00:11:02,380 --> 00:11:03,320
Now, go do it."
现在，去做吧。”

116
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:11,048
And that's just what I'm going to say to Wisconsin.
这就是我要对威斯康星州说的话。

117
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:11,940
Message received.
收到消息。

118
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:20,560
So, to every member of the legislation, Democrat or Republican, my door is always open.
因此，对于每一位立法委员，无论是民主党人还是共和党人，我的大门永远敞开。

119
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:28,460
Starting tomorrow morning, I'm going to sit down with anyone who is serious about lowering costs for our working families.
从明天早上开始，我将与任何认真考虑降低工薪家庭成本的人一起坐下来。

120
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:36,320
We won't agree on everything, but we don't have to agree on everything in order to agree on something.
我们不会在所有事情上都达成一致，但我们不必为了在某些事情上达成一致而在所有事情上都达成一致。

121
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:40,920
And there's a whole lot of something that needs to be done and waiting to be done,
还有很多事情需要完成并等待完成，

122
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,820
And this is why we have to get it done.
这就是为什么我们必须完成它。

123
00:11:43,478 --> 00:11:55,880
So, I remain optimistic that tonight we will see Democratic majorities.
因此，我仍然乐观地认为今晚我们将看到民主党获得多数席位。

124
00:11:55,880 --> 00:12:03,728
And for the first time since 2010, Wisconsin voters will trust us to lead.
自 2010 年以来，威斯康星州选民第一次信任我们的领导能力。

125
00:12:03,738 --> 00:12:06,730
Pro-worker just would mean we earn that trust every day.
支持工人意味着我们每天都赢得这种信任。

126
00:12:07,458 --> 00:12:09,630
And we do it by governing the whole state.
我们通过管理整个州来做到这一点。

127
00:12:10,978 --> 00:12:16,218
But still, the people of Wisconsin elected me as their governor.
但威斯康星州人民仍然选举我担任他们的州长。

128
00:12:16,228 --> 00:12:34,279
It's It is my responsibility to offer my vision where we are headed and to provide the leadership to bring us together and to Get it done.
我的责任是提出我的愿景，并领导我们团结起来，实现我们的目标。完成它。

129
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:38,010
So, here's the work that I intend to do on your behalf.
所以，这就是我打算代表您做的工作。

130
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:44,733
We're going to lower costs for housing, utilities, and for child care.
我们将降低住房、公用事业和儿童保育的成本。

131
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:47,610
We're going to bring real property tax relief.
我们将实行不动产税减免。

132
00:12:48,690 --> 00:12:53,730
We're going to provide health care that you can that is both accessible and affordable,
我们将提供您力所能及的医疗保健，既方便又负担得起，

133
00:12:54,350 --> 00:12:55,490
But with real options.
但有真实的选择。

134
00:12:56,450 --> 00:13:00,430
Good schools funded without a referendum every other year.
好学校无需每隔一年进行一次公民投票即可获得资助。

135
00:13:01,010 --> 00:13:04,910
A government that is open, accountable, and transparent.
一个开放、负责、透明的政府。

136
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:06,650
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

137
00:13:07,730 --> 00:13:10,730
None of these are Democratic or Republican ideas.
这些都不是民主党或共和党的想法。

138
00:13:11,610 --> 00:13:13,370
These are Wisconsin ideas, y'all.
这些是威斯康星州的想法，你们大家。

139
00:13:13,370 --> 00:13:19,350
And for those of us who are headed to Madison in January, our job is to get it done.
对于我们这些一月份前往麦迪逊的人来说，我们的工作就是完成它。

140
00:13:20,430 --> 00:13:24,670
And many of you know that our state's motto is just one word.
你们中的许多人都知道我们州的座右铭只是一个词。

141
00:13:26,090 --> 00:13:27,570
It's right here on our flag.
它就在我们的旗帜上。

142
00:13:28,299 --> 00:13:29,110
Y'all know what that is?
你们都知道那是什么吗？

143
00:13:30,379 --> 00:13:31,544
Forward.
向前。

144
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:38,260
That word doesn't just belong to one party or one election.
这个词不仅仅属于一个政党或一次选举。

145
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:46,369
It belongs to the dairy farmer in Marathon County and the nurse finish finishing a double shift right here in Milwaukee.
它属于马拉松县的奶农，护士在密尔沃基完成了两班倒。

146
00:13:46,379 --> 00:13:51,020
It belongs to our elderly elderly neighbors who've gotten us to this place.
它属于我们年老的邻居，是他们把我们带到了这个地方。

147
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:56,929
And even every young person who's in this room who inherit what we build next.
甚至在座的每一个年轻人都继承了我们接下来要建立的东西。

148
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:04,800
It belongs to the young kids somewhere in our state facing eviction and struggling who knows he or she may one day become governor.
它属于我们州某个地方面临驱逐和挣扎的年轻孩子，他们知道自己有一天可能会成为州长。

149
00:14:07,215 --> 00:14:12,889
Tomorrow Tomorrow the signs will come down.
明天 明天，迹象就会降下来。

150
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,640
The ads will finally stop.
广告终于会停止了。

151
00:14:17,404 --> 00:14:25,386
And we will go back to being what we always once were, neighbors.
我们将回到以前的样子，邻居。

152
00:14:25,930 --> 00:14:27,890
So, let's show the country how it's done.
那么，让我们向全国展示它是如何做到的。

153
00:14:28,610 --> 00:14:35,079
In a world that is all too divided, let's buck the trend in true Wisconsin fashion, Y'all.
在一个过于分裂的世界里，让我们以真正的威斯康星州时尚逆流而上，你们大家。

154
00:14:35,089 --> 00:14:39,390
Let's be the state where elections make us better, not bitter.
让我们成为一个选举让我们变得更好而不是痛苦的国家。

155
00:14:39,990 --> 00:14:45,990
Where we stop asking where idea came from, and instead ask, "Where will it take us?"
我们不再问想法从何而来，而是问“它将带我们去往何方？”

156
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:51,320
The great vince lombardi once said, "people who work together will win."
伟大的文斯·隆巴尔迪曾经说过：“齐心协力的人就会胜利。”

157
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:57,360
Whether it be against complex football defenses or the problems of modern society.
无论是面对复杂的足球防守还是现代社会的问题。

158
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:01,640
People who work together will win.
共同努力的人们将会获胜。

159
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:08,131
Not Democrats, not Republicans, but people, y'all.
不是民主党人，不是共和党人，而是人民。

160
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:13,070
And I learned that people need money power each and every single day.
我了解到人们每天都需要金钱的力量。

161
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:18,211
And so, my fellow Wisconsinites, we are not a red state.
因此，我的威斯康星州同胞们，我们不是一个红色州。

162
00:15:18,221 --> 00:15:20,891
We are not a blue state.
我们不是蓝州。

163
00:15:20,901 --> 00:15:24,011
We are not defined by rural and urban.
我们不以农村和城市来定义。

164
00:15:24,021 --> 00:15:27,681
We are one people, one Wisconsin.
我们是一个人，一个威斯康星州。

165
00:15:27,681 --> 00:15:33,171
And tonight, we choose to move forward together, Y'all.
今晚，我们选择一起前进，你们大家。

166
00:15:33,181 --> 00:15:34,931
God bless Wisconsin.
上帝保佑威斯康星州。

167
00:15:34,941 --> 00:15:36,611
God bless you all.
上帝保佑你们大家。

168
00:15:36,621 --> 00:15:38,371
And let's get to work.
让我们开始工作吧。

169
00:15:38,381 --> 00:15:38,615
Thank you.
谢谢你。
